            <ArticleTitle>[An uncommon cutaneous presentation of cat scratch disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>614-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.annder.2013.04.080</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0151-9638(13)00756-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Herein we report a case of cat scratch disease on account of its atypical presentation.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENTS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 21-year-old woman presented erythema nodosum associated with painful bilateral inguinal adenopathy, odynophagia, joint pain and evening urticaria in a setting of impaired general condition. Initial serological testing for Bartonella henselae was negative. PCR for Bartonella henselae performed on an adenectomy fragment was positive. A favourable outcome was achieved with azithromycin.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="COMMENTS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This case shows an atypical and severe presentation of cat scratch disease and raises the problem of sensitivity of serotyping.</AbstractText>
